"answer": "Sudden cardiac arrest (SCA) and a heart attack differ primarily in their mechanism and effect on heart function. SCA is an electrical problem where the heart suddenly stops beating, causing blood flow to cease [MLP-4266]. In contrast, a heart attack is a circulation problem where blood flow to the heart is blocked, but the heart usually continues to beat [MLP-4266]. While a heart attack can sometimes lead to SCA, they are distinct events [MLP-4266]."
}
